# Architecture

## Repository layout

```
rentACar/
├── apps/
│   ├── api/                    # NestJS backend
│   │   ├── prisma/
│   │   └── src/
│   │       ├── modules/        # one folder per domain feature
│   │       ├── common/         # guards, filters, pipes, decorators
│   │       └── config/
│   └── mobile/                 # React Native CLI
│       └── src/
│           ├── features/       # feature screens, hooks, local components
│           ├── components/     # shared reusable UI
│           ├── theme/          # design tokens, colors, typography, spacing
│           ├── api/            # API client, TanStack Query hooks/keys
│           └── stores/         # Zustand stores (client-only state)
└── packages/
    └── shared/                 # shared types/constants (optional, when needed)
```

When scaffolding, follow this layout. Do not invent alternate top-level structures without strong reason.

## Principles

- **Feature-based modules** — group by domain (`rentals`, `vehicles`, `handovers`, `ratings`), not by technical layer only.
- **Separation of concerns**:
  - Controllers/handlers: HTTP only — no business logic.
  - Services: business rules and orchestration.
  - Repositories/Prisma layer: data access only.
  - Mobile screens: composition; logic in hooks/services.
- **Reusable components** — extract shared UI to `components/` or `theme/`; feature-specific UI stays in `features/<name>/`.
- **Single source of truth** — rental/handover state lives on the backend; mobile reflects server state via TanStack Query.
- **Extensibility** — design boundaries (interfaces, module exports) so future payments/subscriptions plug in without coupling to rental state machine.

## API ↔ mobile contract

- RESTful JSON APIs with consistent response envelopes and error shapes.
- Version endpoints under `/api/v1/` when the API is introduced.
- Shared DTO shapes may live in `packages/shared` to avoid drift between backend and mobile.
